 # InNeRF360
 
-Also called: InNeRF360
 
 ## Overview
-InNeRF360 is a method for 3D scene inpainting and editing that combines multiview-consistent 2D priors with 3D diffusion guidance to reconstruct missing or edited regions in a Neural Radiance Field (NeRF). It addresses the problem of generating geometrically and photometrically consistent content for occluded or removed objects by first establishing a coherent 2D inpainting across all views and then refining the 3D representation. It differs from direct 3D optimization methods by decoupling the generation of plausible content (via 2D inpainting) from the 3D reconstruction, using 3D diffusion priors primarily to eliminate artifacts and enforce consistency rather than generating the primary geometry.
+InNeRF360 is a 3D scene inpainting and editing method that reconstructs missing or edited regions in a Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) by combining multiview-consistent 2D priors with 3D diffusion guidance [S1]. It addresses the problem of generating geometrically and photometrically consistent content for occluded or removed objects by first establishing a coherent 2D inpainting across all views and then refining the 3D representation [S1]. It differs from direct 3D optimization methods by decoupling the generation of plausible content (via 2D inpainting) from the 3D reconstruction, using 3D diffusion priors primarily to eliminate artifacts and enforce consistency rather than generating the primary geometry [S1].
 
